            "primary_use": "Carminative, digestive",
            "grieve_excerpt": "Description. It is a biennial, with smooth, furrowed stems, growing 14 to 2 feet high, bearing finely cut leaves, and umbels of white flowers which blossom in June. The fruits \u2014 which are popularly and incorrectly called seeds-\u2014and which correspond in general character to those of the other plants of this large family, are laterally compressed, somewhat horny and translucent, slightly curved, and marked with five distinct, pale ridges. They evolve a pleasant, aromatic odour when bruised, and have an agreeable taste. The leaves possess similar properties and afford an oil identical with that of",
