            "primary_use": "Carminative, galactagogue",
            "grieve_excerpt": "Description. Herbaceous perennial plant, composite, distinguished by a naked re- ceptacle, oblong, imbricated, involucre, and a feathery pappus, fleshy basal leaves obo- lanceolate, terminating in a flattened stalk. Leaves of stem clasping at base. The leaves are used to flavour tobacco. Their perfume is largely due to Coumarin, which can be seen in crystals on the upper side of the smooth spatulate leaves. Most of the species are used medicinally, Medicinal Action and Uses. Demulcent, febrifuge, diaphoretic. DELPHINIUM. See LARKSPUR, STAVESACRE DEVIL\u2019S BIT. See scasious DILL ",
            "grieve_search_term": "DILL",
            "source_planet_metal": "Culpeper 1653 + Lilly 1647 (public domain)",
            "source_grieve": "Grieve 1931 A Modern Herbal (public domain, IA: herbal-dictionary)"
