            "primary_use": "Childbirth, uterine (historical)",
            "grieve_excerpt": "Description. There are several species of the Aristolochias used by herbalists in India. \u2018The root is spindle-shaped from 5 cm. to 3 dm. in length, about 2 cm. in thickness, fleshy, very brittle, greyish externally, brown- ish-yellow inside, bitter and of a strong dis- agreeable odour when fresh. 4 Constituent, Aristolochine. q Medicinal Action and Uses. Said to be use- ful as an aromatic stimulant in rheumatism and gout and for removing obstructions, etc., after childbirth. Dose, $ to 1 drachm of the powdered root. g Other Species. Aristolochia, cymbifera from Brazil and Mexico is said to hav",
